<title>UK: Aluminium stocks rise in March - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks rise in March - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, rose to 3.096 million tonnes at the end of March 1997, compared with 3.077 million in February and 3.596 million in March 1996, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks rose to 1.562 million tonnes versus 1.552 million and 1.985 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Mar 97   Feb 97    Mar 96</p>
<p>    Africa		    64	 65	  87</p>
<p>    North America	1,473    1,466     1,712</p>
<p>    Latin America	  152	137	 214</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	135	178	 167</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,133    1,110     1,274</p>
<p>    Oceania		  139	121	 142</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Mar 97   Feb 97    Mar 96</p>
<p>    Africa		    20	 17	  42</p>
<p>    North America	  632	635	 815</p>
<p>    Latin America	  102	 88	 169</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	 98	137	 146</p>
<p>    Europe		   614	593	 709</p>
<p>    Oceania		   96	 82	 104</p>
</text>
